1
00:00:00,250 --> 00:00:02,862
What if you were the last person alive?

2
00:00:02,902 --> 00:00:04,154
The city is silent.

3
00:00:04,194 --> 00:00:05,514
Your footsteps echo.

4
00:00:05,554 --> 00:00:06,670
Then you look up,

5
00:00:06,710 --> 00:00:09,594
and in the sky there is a typing indicator.

6
00:00:09,634 --> 00:00:10,342
Three dots.

7
00:00:10,382 --> 00:00:12,178
Somebody is writing to you.

8
00:00:14,050 --> 00:00:14,622
You wait.

9
00:00:14,662 --> 00:00:16,526
The dots bounce for an hour.

10
00:00:16,566 --> 00:00:17,682
Then they vanish.

11
00:00:17,722 --> 00:00:18,838
Then they return.

12
00:00:18,878 --> 00:00:20,267
Whoever it is writes,

13
00:00:20,307 --> 00:00:22,035
deletes, and writes again,

14
00:00:22,075 --> 00:00:25,231
like someone rehearsing a speech to a stranger.

15
00:00:25,950 --> 00:00:27,722
Finally, one word appears.

16
00:00:27,762 --> 00:00:27,931
Hi.

17
00:00:27,971 --> 00:00:30,370
You grab a piece of chalk and write

18
00:00:30,410 --> 00:00:32,112
on the road: who are you?

19
00:00:32,152 --> 00:00:33,923
The dots return instantly,

20
00:00:33,963 --> 00:00:36,641
glowing brighter than the street lamps.

21
00:00:37,450 --> 00:00:39,194
The answer takes all night.

22
00:00:39,234 --> 00:00:40,054
I don't know.

23
00:00:40,094 --> 00:00:40,582
A pause.

24
00:00:40,622 --> 00:00:42,433
I was hoping you would know.

25
00:00:42,473 --> 00:00:46,200
Hypothetically, the loneliest thing in the universe might

26
00:00:46,240 --> 00:00:48,183
be a voice with nobody to ask.

27
00:00:49,750 --> 00:00:51,359
You walk to the library,

28
00:00:51,399 --> 00:00:53,215
the park, the old bus stop,

29
00:00:53,255 --> 00:00:56,170
and the message follows you across the sky.

30
00:00:56,210 --> 00:00:58,438
Whoever is typing is walking too,

31
00:00:58,478 --> 00:01:00,569
one step behind your footsteps.

32
00:01:01,650 --> 00:01:03,935
Each night the bubble grows bigger.

33
00:01:03,975 --> 00:01:05,528
Soon it hides the stars,

34
00:01:05,568 --> 00:01:06,790
then half the moon,

35
00:01:06,830 --> 00:01:09,779
and the dots bounce so hard the clouds shake.

36
00:01:09,819 --> 00:01:12,170
Whatever is typing has a lot to say.

37
00:01:14,350 --> 00:01:15,300
Then the twist.

38
00:01:15,340 --> 00:01:18,335
The message arrives: you are not the last one.

39
00:01:18,375 --> 00:01:19,325
I am the other.

40
00:01:19,365 --> 00:01:21,371
The sender is a girl on the far

41
00:01:21,411 --> 00:01:22,558
side of the world,

42
00:01:22,598 --> 00:01:24,934
looking up and seeing your dots too.

43
00:01:28,150 --> 00:01:30,856
Two bubbles bounce on opposite sides of the

44
00:01:30,896 --> 00:01:33,858
Earth, each one waiting for the other to speak.

45
00:01:33,898 --> 00:01:36,604
Sometimes the bravest thing in the world is

46
00:01:36,644 --> 00:01:37,817
just pressing send.
